  "verbalization": "Debromohymenialdisine appears to have a complex network of targets, with Casein kinase I delta being a downstream target in two distinct pathways. The first pathway links Debromohymenialdisine to Leukocyte antigen CD37, which is then targeted by Mitrekaurenone, and finally targets Casein kinase I delta. The second pathway connects Debromohymenialdisine to Mono-ADP-ribosyltransferase C3, which is targeted by a complex compound and ultimately also targets Casein kinase I delta. Both pathways suggest that Debromohymenialdisine may influence Casein kinase I delta through different intermediate targets. The integration of these pathways implies that Debromohymenialdisine could exert its effects on Casein kinase I delta via multiple mechanisms, possibly through distinct molecular interactions. The evidence supports a potential role for Debromohymenialdisine in modulating Casein kinase I delta, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
